// span-kind-coverage.kql
// Description: Counts spans by OpenInference span kind over the last hour, to confirm every
// expected span kind (CHAIN, TOOL, LLM) is present and no kind is silently missing from the
// synthetic demo traffic. Retry-attempt spans (which carry no openinference.span.kind) surface
// under the "" (empty string) bucket, which is itself useful drift signal if its count diverges
// unexpectedly from the number of llm.chat_completion.attempt rows.
// Expected output shape: a table with columns [kind, spanCount], one row per distinct span kind
// seen (including one row for "" if any retry-attempt spans exist in the window), each with a
// non-zero count for a healthy synthetic run.
AppDependencies
| where timestamp > ago(1h)
| summarize spanCount = count() by kind = tostring(customDimensions["openinference.span.kind"])
| order by spanCount desc
